venus: share memory through AHardwareBuffers on Android

A driver that imports dma-bufs but exports no fd (Mali on Google Tensor exports AHardwareBuffers
only) left vkAllocateMemory with no allocator: gbm and udmabuf do not exist on Android. Gralloc
allocates a BLOB AHardwareBuffer instead; its dma-buf is imported into Vulkan and kept for the
blob export the guest maps or passes on.

- Host-visible coherent allocations (the ones the guest maps), and every allocation the guest
  wants to export as a dma-buf whatever its type, take that route. Cached non-coherent types,
  which the guest hides as device-local, are allocated directly.
- Because exports take it, dma-buf export is offered for explicit-modifier image queries where
  the driver reports dma-buf import: a compositor in the guest can export its output. Not for
  buffers or other images: the guest cannot import a dma-buf over vtest, so an app exporting to
  re-import its own memory is better told there is no export.
- The guest maps the pages without cache maintenance, so cached gralloc usage is asked for only
  where the driver's type is cached; the dma-buf exporter gralloc picked is logged once per kind.
- The dma-buf's size is checked before import; a memory type the driver will not import gralloc
  memory into fails with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE (logged once per type) instead of an
  invalid import; the kept fd is closed when the import fails.

Binary files pa/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/__pycache__/u_format_parse.cpython-313.pyc and pb/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/__pycache__/u_format_parse.cpython-313.pyc differ
